    "result_text": "The full test suite passes with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the daily owner-creation limit in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (the sole `POST /api/owners` handler).\n\n**Changes to `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:**\n\n1. Added a `DAILY_CREATE_LIMIT = 100` constant and an `ownersRegisteredOn(LocalDate)` helper that counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals a given day \u2014 mirroring the existing `cityOwnerCount` / `CITY_CAPACITY` pattern.\n\n2. In `addOwner`, computed the effective registration date (the request's value if present, otherwise `LocalDate.now()`) and, before saving, returned **429 Too Many Requests** when 100 or more owners already carry that date:\n   ```java\n   if (ownersRegisteredOn(registrationDate) >= DAILY_CREATE_LIMIT) {\n       return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.TOO_MANY_REQUESTS);\n   }\n   ```\n\n3. Reused that computed date when persisting the owner, replacing the previous inline null-check so the counted date and the stored date always agree.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsOverDailyLimit` test (create 100 owners dated today, expect the 101st to be rejected with 429) passes, along with the rest of the suite.",
